\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
All IB features at a glance.
 The reward is not part of the GP-process.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Industrial Benchmark was introduced by scientists at Siemens to meet
 the high requirements of complex, real world industrial processes.
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "industrialBenchmark"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 It is high-dimensional 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset

, yet the Markov process is only partially observable, so even past values
 must also be considered.
 Since it is also very stochastic, the learning process is made even more
 difficult.
 The Reward depends on a combination of Action 0 and Action 1, as well as
 Action 2, which severely penalises misconduct.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Currently there are no good human written solutions known for the IB, but
 approaching the average value (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

do nothing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) is considered to be a respectably good comparison solution.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Black box: PSONN
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As black box, a particle swarm optimisation algorithm with neural networks
 (PSONN 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "PSONN_fuzzy_RL_Hein_Udluft"
literal "true"

\end_inset

) with a calculated IB reward of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$5353$
\end_layout

\end_inset

 was chosen.
 
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The initial states of the IB in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 were randomized.
 Comparable values could be obtained by a randomized initial state, but
 the results were very volatile.
 The difference of agents in Hein's work was 7% worse on average.
 This value was used for comparison.
 For the PSONN policy, this results in a adjusted penalty value of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$5728/1.07=5353$
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Particle swarm optimisation algorithms, similar to GP, can find solutions
 for many types of problems.
 The solution space is populated by a swarm population, which should find
 the best optima by swarm intelligence.
 This approach is very interesting as a black box, because even bulky solution
 models can be found relatively quickly.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Comparison
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A separate run was started for each of the three actions of the IB, whose
 generated candidates are in turn merged on a combined Pareto front.
 Action 0 is extremely difficult to achieve; in most runs the regression
 error of 0.8 was about 30% higher than for the rest.
\end_layout

