\begin_layout Subsection
IB summary
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The regression error of no run was able to reach the neuropolicy data set
 sufficiently; for MSE runs the limit was about 2, for MAE runs about 1.5.
 Thus even the best candidates are about 5 times worse than comparable candidate
s of the MC benchmark.
 There can be many reasons for this poor performance, the most likely being
 that the PSONN policy is too complex as a black box to be sufficiently
 approximated by genetic programming.
 This is also confirmed by the results of 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, where the regression error also did not fall significantly below a limit
 of 2.
 Since the candidates cannot expect any performance gain, their evaluation
 would not be meaningful.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\noindent
\align center
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename ../benchmarks/slurm_runs/MTC200_MSE_scratch/histograms/acthist_25.pdf
	height 5cm

\end_inset


\begin_inset Graphics
	filename C:/Users/Rapid/PycharmProjects/plagih/benchmarks/slurm_runs2/IB_MSE_scratch/IB_MSE_scratch_0/histograms/acthist_29.pdf
	height 5cm

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Histograms for the deviation from the target action for the Mountain car
 (left) and the Industrial benchmark (right).
 In both cases the best regular GP candidate, calculated with the MSE, was
 chosen.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The PSONN policy that was used as the black box for the IB is already too
 different at the beginning of each expert policy tested to allow for any
 hope of improvement.
 Knowledge about the strategy that PSONN was pursuing could therefore not
 be gained - at best, it is a very complex approach that can hardly be represent
ed by simple formulas.
 All GP races were too similar in their real fitness and safety to allow
 conclusions and fell far short of results trained on the real benchmark.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Normal GP results had no real advantages over the familiar results despite
 their enhanced familiarity.
 The explanatory candidates were thus able to find the result even with
 the implicitly reduced solution space, which is at least a partial success
 for trust-based GP.
\end_layout

